I have a very limited budget but i need INSTA engagement and influencers to the run up the xmas.

www.themunchclub.com
@munchclub_og

UK-based applicants only. You must currently live in the United Kingdom.

We are a London construction company looking for a reliable and confident person to help us make professional telephone calls to architects, interior designers and other relevant businesses.

The main part of the work is speaking to people by phone, introducing our company, building a good relationship and helping us get considered for future projects and tender opportunities.

This is not mainly an email or marketing role. We need someone who is comfortable spending the working time actually talking to people on the phone.

You do not need to come from the construction industry. We will explain our company, our services and what information you need to communicate.

What is important is that you:

* have previous experience speaking professionally with customers or businesses by telephone;
* are confident, friendly and able to build rapport;
* can communicate clearly and professionally;
* are comfortable speaking with architects, designers and business owners;
* can work from home during weekday mornings;
* are reliable and able to work agreed hours consistently.

The role is initially around 4–6 hours per week, normally during weekday mornings.

Pay: £15–£25 per hour depending on experience, plus a performance-based bonus.

Experience in B2B calls, sales, customer service, appointment setting or business development would be useful, but construction experience is not essential.

InEnergy Ltd is a UK business energy consultancy looking for an experienced B2B Appointment Setter / SDR to generate qualified appointments with UK business decision-makers.

This is a consultative outbound role. We are looking for someone who can speak confidently with business owners, directors and finance teams, identify genuine electricity or gas opportunities, understand basic renewal timing and book worthwhile appointments.

Our Managing Director will handle the detailed consultation, proposal, negotiation and close.

Experience required

Previous UK B2B cold-calling experience is essential.

Business energy or utilities experience would be an advantage, but we will also consider strong candidates from telecoms, finance, insurance or other consultative B2B sectors.

You should be confident with:

cold calling and gatekeepers;

reaching decision-makers;

qualifying genuine opportunities;

asking sensible questions around suppliers and renewal dates;

booking quality appointments;

keeping clear notes and follow-up actions.

We are interested in quality, not simply call volume.

Working pattern

Initial 4-week engagement:

around 6 hours per week;

preferably Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday;

approximately 2 hours per day;

£20+ per hour depending on experience.

There is potential for increased hours and an ongoing relationship if the campaign performs well.

Calls will be made through an InEnergy-controlled calling system and may be recorded for quality, training and compliance purposes.

InEnergy will provide prospect data and systems.

To apply

Please briefly tell us:

your UK B2B appointment-setting experience;

sectors you have worked in;

any energy/utilities experience;

examples of results achieved;

your hourly rate and availability;

whether you are comfortable using a company-controlled recorded calling system.

A short voice sample or example call recording would also be helpful.

We are looking for someone who can represent InEnergy professionally and consistently create genuine sales opportunities, not just diary bookings.
